    "created_at": "2018-05-30T04:32:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-05-30T04:32:13Z",
    "body": "Yes, I'll get on the HTTP Archive (hopefully will have time in the next few days). @annevk the motivation for this is mostly that while implementing https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/3678 in Chromium, I came across an enum we keep around, whose members indicate whether we're respecting legacy values or not. I was wondering if it would be possible to remove support for legacy values, which brought me here. I understand motivation for not wanting to drop support (like you said it really doesn't cost us), but if it would be considered once I get some data then I'll move forward. Else we can close this.",
